## Summary

Implemented PRD-083 (Reachable Approval — the Decidable Pause) in `crates/familiar-ai-daemon`:

**Core changes:**
- **`stewardship.rs`**: added `scope_decision_commands()` (the exact approve/reject `scope-decisions` lines, hash-bound, with `human:<identity>` placeholder) and `scope_pause_notices()`; `list_pending_human_gates` now prepends scope commands ahead of release/complete/resume recovery commands whenever a gate has a pending scope decision.
- **`report.rs`**: `render_judgment` now prints each stopped attempt's approve/reject commands before its `backlog release`/`backlog complete` lines.
- **`cli/scope_decisions.rs`**: rewrote the bare invocation into `list_or_decide_interactively` — a numbered, hash-free listing (PRD, change, finding) that takes a decision by ordinal or PRD id, with actor and reason both validated identically to the flag path. This same function is shared with the drive's pause.
- **`drive.rs`**: added `handle_scope_pause` — invokes the interactive picker when attended, otherwise prints paste-runnable approve **and** reject commands. Wired into the real pause site with real terminal detection.
- **`cli/next.rs`** / **`resume.rs`**: when blocked or resuming, both now surface any pending scope decision's exact commands (not in `expected_files`, but required by the acceptance criteria — noted as a scope addition).
- **`cli/stewardship.rs`**: doc-comment update only.

**Incidental fix:** `main.rs`'s `run_with_tray_feature_but_disabled` had a pre-existing (already-committed, unrelated to this PRD) call to `daemon_run` missing the `&mut TerminationSignals` argument added by an earlier commit — this broke compilation of every test target in the crate (and the whole workspace's `--all-targets`). Fixed minimally by mirroring the correct call site, since it blocked verifying this PRD's own work.

**Tests:** new `tests/scope_approval_ux.rs` (12 tests) pins all five acceptance criteria directly, including an attended-picker regression driven via injected `BufRead`/`Write` (no real TTY needed) and a flag-vs-interactive row-equivalence test. All 135 pre-existing lib tests plus the full existing integration suite remain green (verified with `--no-default-features` to route around an unrelated missing system library, `libxdo`, needed only for the optional tray feature). `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy` are clean except one pre-existing, unrelated warning in `familiar-ai-core`.

No acceptance criteria are outstanding.
