## Summary

PRD-087 is fully implemented. All five acceptance criteria are met, verified by real regression tests, and each was confirmed to fail loudly (mutation-tested by hand) when its underlying fix was temporarily reverted.

**What was found:** repository identity was actually being minted independently in *three* places (`backlog.rs`, `config/context_service.rs`, and `daemon/run.rs`), each shelling out to `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` separately — kept in sync only by a code comment. Checkpoint/occurrence event-sequence numbering was similarly duplicated across four writers (`checkpoint.rs`'s `put`/`transition`, storage `backlog.rs`'s `approve_and_complete`, and two landing paths in `daemon/drive.rs`).

**What changed:**
- `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/repository_path.rs` — new single minting site: `repository_origin_key`/`git_common_directory`.
- `backlog.rs`, `config/context_service.rs`, `daemon/run.rs` — now delegate instead of duplicating.
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/worktree.rs` — `origin_repository_key` for worktree-origin resolution.
- `crates/familiar-ai-storage/src/repos/checkpoint.rs` — single `next_checkpoint_event_id` allocator, used by all four writers (`backlog.rs`, `drive.rs` updated accordingly).
- `crates/familiar-ai-storage/migrations/061_identity_invariants.sql` (+ `migrate.rs` registration) — real `sequence` column with a `UNIQUE(checkpoint_id, sequence)` index, backfilled from existing rows; new `identity_invariant_tolerances` audit ledger.
- `crates/familiar-ai-storage/src/repos/review.rs` — pre-existing FAM-BUG-032 tolerance now also records itself to the ledger.
- `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/tests/durable_invariants.rs` (new) — the four required regressions, each naming its invariant on failure.
- `docs/running_bugs.md` — new ledger-linkage section, checked byte-for-byte by the test above.
- Collateral: 8 migration-count literals in `migrate.rs` bumped by the new migration (verified against actual counts, not guessed).

**Verification:** `cargo fmt --check` clean; `clippy -D warnings` clean except two pre-existing warnings in untouched files (`bootstrap.rs`, `summary_worker.rs`); full `familiar-ai-core`/`familiar-ai-storage`/`familiar-ai-daemon` suites green in isolation. Two load-dependent timing flakes surfaced under full-workspace parallel load (`drive::tests::progress_heartbeat_...`, `worktree::tests::missing_ownership_record_...`) — both pre-existing (unrelated code, reproduce with `git stash`, pass cleanly standalone), matching the exact flake class already documented as FAM-BUG-047/030/033.

**Pre-existing issue found but not touched (out of scope):** `familiar-ai-daemon/src/main.rs` fails to compile only with the default `tray` feature (a stale call to `daemon_run`); the project's actual gate builds `--no-default-features`, where it's unaffected. Confirmed pre-existing via `git stash`.
